course: dictionary
lesson: 15454
title: Stimulant: a word that wakes things up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stimulant is something that makes your body or brain more awake and active for a while. Context helps you spot it. «Coffee and cola contain caffeine, a stimulant.» Caffeine is a stimulant, so it is something that wakes you up.
explain: The word can also mean something that gets things going or growing faster. «The new park was a stimulant to the whole town.» The park brought people out and helped the town grow. Try your meaning in the sentence: "something that gets the town going" still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: Some stimulants are strong drugs and can be harmful. «Energy drinks contain stimulants and are not meant for children.» Words like harmful and not meant for children are clues that this is a warning. When a word appears in a warning, read the warning carefully.
fact: A stimulant makes your body or brain more awake and active for a while.
fact: Caffeine, found in coffee, tea and cola, is a common stimulant.
fact: Some stimulants are used as medicine, some are illegal, and some can be harmful.
fact: Energy drinks contain stimulants, and they are not meant for children.
fact: A stimulant can also be something that gets things going faster, such as a stimulant to the imagination.
exercise: «Caffeine is a stimulant, so a cup of cola can make you feel more awake.» What is a stimulant? | *Something that makes your body or brain more awake and active | A sweet food for breakfast | Something that makes you cold | Something that makes you sleepy
exercise: «Energy drinks contain stimulants and are not meant for children.» Why are they not meant for children? | They are only for sport | Children need them to sleep | *Stimulants can be harmful, and children should not have them | They taste nice
exercise: «The new park was a stimulant to the whole town.» What does stimulant mean in this sentence? | A dangerous road | Something that is always quiet | *Something that gets things going or growing faster | A type of medicine for the head
test: «Some stimulants are used as medicine.» Which statement is true? | Stimulants make you fall asleep at once | Every stimulant is a sweet food | Stimulants are only found in fruit | *Some stimulants are used as medicine
test: «Some stimulants are banned in sport.» Why might a sports rule ban a stimulant? | Because it is too cheap | Because it makes the team happy | *Because the rules do not allow it in sport | Because it tastes bad
exam: «Caffeine is a mild stimulant, so it wakes you up a little.» What does mild suggest? | *Gentle, not very strong | Full of sugar | Cold and wet | Very strong and harmful
